---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { SITE_NAME, SITE_DOMAIN, SITE_URL, LAST_UPDATED, CONTACT_EMAIL } from '../config/siteInfo';

const pageTitle = `Terms & Conditions — ${SITE_NAME}`;
const pageDescription = `Terms and Conditions for ${SITE_DOMAIN}. Independent browser-based software project. U.S.-relevant accuracy disclaimer, DMCA procedure (17 U.S.C. § 512), limitation of liability.`;
const canonicalURL = `${SITE_URL}/terms/`;
---

<Layout title={pageTitle} description={pageDescription} canonicalURL={canonicalURL}>
  <main class="ror-main">
    <div class="ror-container">
      <div class="ror-back-row">
        <a href="/" class="ror-back-link">&larr; Back to {SITE_NAME}</a>
      </div>

      <h1 class="ror-h1">Terms &amp; Conditions</h1>
      <p class="ror-updated">Last updated: {LAST_UPDATED}</p>

      <p class="ror-intro-copy">
        Please read these Terms and Conditions ("Terms") carefully before using <a href={SITE_URL} class="ror-link">{SITE_DOMAIN}</a> ("the Service"). By accessing or using the Service, you agree to be bound by these Terms. Instanten is an independent browser-based software project, not a registered U.S. corporation with a physical office.
      </p>

      <section class="ror-section">
        <h2 class="ror-h2">1. Use of the Service</h2>
        <p class="ror-p">
          {SITE_NAME} is a free directory and utility site providing <strong>instant tools</strong>, <strong>instant help</strong> guides, and practical resources. You may access and use the Service at no cost ($0) and without creating an account. The Service includes curated tool listings, free online utilities (Online Ruler, Image Compressor, JSON Formatter, Base64 Encoder, Color Palette, CSS Grid Generator, Markdown Editor, Meta Tag Generator, and others), and step-by-step guides.
        </p>
        <p class="ror-p">You agree not to:</p>
        <ul class="ror-ul">
          <li>Use the Service for any unlawful purpose or to violate any applicable U.S. federal, state, or local law.</li>
          <li>Attempt to interfere with, damage, or gain unauthorized access to the Service or its infrastructure.</li>
          <li>Scrape, crawl, or extract content programmatically without explicit written permission.</li>
          <li>Use any tool output as a substitute for certified professional advice in medical, legal, financial, or structural engineering contexts.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="ror-section">
        <h2 class="ror-h2">2. Accuracy &amp; Non-Critical Use Disclaimer</h2>
        <p class="ror-p">
          The tools, calculators, utilities, and guides provided on {SITE_DOMAIN} are browser-based productivity aids for informational and practical purposes only. They are <strong>not substitutes</strong> for certified NIST-traceable physical measurement instruments, qualified medical diagnosis, licensed legal advice, certified financial analysis, or professional structural engineering evaluation. Outputs and recommendations may vary based on input quality, browser environment, operating system, screen calibration, and other external factors.
        </p>
        <ul class="ror-ul">
          <li>Results from online tools depend on the accuracy and format of your inputs.</li>
          <li>Guides reflect best practices at the time of publication and may not cover every scenario.</li>
          <li>The <strong>Online Ruler</strong> is a visual browser utility for quick measurement estimation — not a certified NIST-traceable physical ruler or engineering-grade instrument. For critical measurements requiring certified traceability, use a certified physical instrument.</li>
          <li>The <strong>Color Palette</strong> contrast ratios follow W3C WCAG 2.2 Level AA formulas (4.5:1 normal text, 3:1 large text) for reference — always verify accessibility with official testing tools for production U.S. websites requiring ADA Title III or Section 508 compliance.</li>
          <li>The <strong>JSON Formatter</strong> validates syntax according to IETF RFC 8259 rules — it does not guarantee the semantic correctness of data for legal, medical, or financial systems.</li>
          <li>We make <strong>no warranties</strong> regarding the completeness, accuracy, or suitability of any tool output or article content for critical applications.</li>
          <li>For critical business, legal, medical, financial, or engineering decisions, always verify results independently using certified methods and consult qualified professionals.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="ror-section">
        <h2 class="ror-h2">3. Intellectual Property &amp; DMCA Copyright Notice Procedure (17 U.S.C. § 512)</h2>
        <p class="ror-p">
          All original content on {SITE_DOMAIN} — including design, code, copy, guides, and original thumbnails — is owned by {SITE_NAME} or licensed under appropriate terms. Tool names, logos, descriptions, and external links belong to their respective owners.
        </p>
        <p class="ror-p">
          You may not reproduce, distribute, create derivative works from, or commercially exploit our original content without written permission. Fair use for personal, non-commercial reference is permitted in accordance with U.S. copyright law (17 U.S.C. § 107).
        </p>
        <p class="ror-p">
          <strong>DMCA Notice Procedure:</strong> If you believe that content on this site infringes your copyright, submit a DMCA copyright notice through our verified <a href="/contact" class="ror-link">contact form</a> (topic: "Privacy / CCPA / DMCA inquiry"). Your notice must include: (1) identification of the copyrighted work claimed to be infringed, (2) identification of the infringing material with sufficient detail to locate it, (3) your contact information, (4) a statement of good faith belief that the use is not authorized, (5) a statement of accuracy under penalty of perjury, and (6) your physical or electronic signature. We will respond promptly in accordance with <strong>17 U.S.C. § 512</strong>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="ror-section">
        <h2 class="ror-h2">4. Disclaimer of Warranties</h2>
        <p class="ror-p">
          THE SERVICE IS PROVIDED "AS IS" AND "AS AVAILABLE" WITHOUT WARRANTIES OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO MERCHANTABILITY, FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE, AND NON-INFRINGEMENT. We do not warrant that the Service will be uninterrupted, error-free, secure, or free of harmful components. Because Instanten is an independent online software project operated without a registered U.S. corporate entity, we provide no corporate guarantees, no service-level agreements, and no certified accuracy warranties for tool outputs.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="ror-section">
        <h2 class="ror-h2">5. Limitation of Liability</h2>
        <p class="ror-p">
          TO THE MAXIMUM EXTENT PERMITTED BY APPLICABLE U.S. LAW, {SITE_NAME} SHALL NOT BE LIABLE FOR ANY INDIRECT, INCIDENTAL, SPECIAL, CONSEQUENTIAL, OR PUNITIVE DAMAGES ARISING FROM YOUR USE OF THE SERVICE, INCLUDING LOSS OF DATA, PROFITS, REVENUE, OR USE — EVEN IF ADVISED OF THE POSSIBILITY OF SUCH DAMAGES.
        </p>
        <p class="ror-p">
          Our total liability for any claim related to the Service shall not exceed the amount you paid to use the Service (<strong>$0</strong>), since the Service is provided completely free of charge.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="ror-section">
        <h2 class="ror-h2">6. Third-Party Links</h2>
        <p class="ror-p">
          The Service contains links to third-party tool websites ("Tools"). These links are provided for convenience only. We do not control, endorse, or assume responsibility for any Tool's content, privacy practices, operations, or terms. Your use of any external Tool is at your own risk and is subject to that site's own terms, privacy policy, and applicable U.S. and international laws.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="ror-section">
        <h2 class="ror-h2">7. Privacy Reference</h2>
        <p class="ror-p">
          Your use of the Service is also governed by our <a href="/privacy-policy" class="ror-link">Privacy Policy</a>, which explains our commitment to not selling or sharing personal data, our compliance with California CCPA/CPRA and applicable U.S. state privacy laws, our COPPA compliance (15 U.S.C. §§ 6501–6506), and our DMCA notice procedure (17 U.S.C. § 512).
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="ror-section">
        <h2 class="ror-h2">8. Changes to These Terms</h2>
        <p class="ror-p">
          We reserve the right to modify these Terms at any time. Changes are effective immediately upon posting to this page. Continued use of the Service after changes constitutes acceptance of the revised Terms. The "Last updated" date at the top reflects the most recent revision.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="ror-section">
        <h2 class="ror-h2">9. Contact</h2>
        <p class="ror-p">
          Questions about these Terms, DMCA notices, accuracy disclaimers, or privacy concerns? Reach out through our verified <a href="/contact" class="ror-link">contact form</a> (topic: "Privacy / CCPA / DMCA inquiry") or email <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`} class="ror-link">{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>. There is no fake office address, no fake U.S. city/state office, and no fake phone number — only real working channels for real users.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </main>
</Layout>
